      ":question/problem": "Consider two paired random samples $X_{1}, X_{2}, \u2026, X_{9}$ and $Y_{1}, Y_{2}, \u2026, Y_{9}$ of size $n = 9$. It is known that the differences between paired observations $D_{i} = X_{i} - Y_{i}$ are normally distributed with population mean $\u03bc$ and population variance $\u03c3^{2} = 3$.\n\nFill in the missing statements below to construct a $95%$ confidence interval for $\u03bc$.\n\nConsider the random variable\n$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ {{field-1}}\nwhere $X^(\u2015)$ and $Y^(\u2015)$ are the sample means of the given samples.\n\nWe have that\n$N(0.1)$ {{field-2}}"
